            <ArticleTitle>Combined valve replacement and coronary bypass grafting in osteogenesis imperfecta.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1395-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Open cardiac procedures in osteogenesis imperfecta have been associated with a high mortality rate. A patient with osteogenesis imperfecta underwent successful aortic valve replacement and coronary artery bypass grafting along with closure of a patent foramen ovale in preparation for a planned hip replacement.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
